14.steps:
1.Open the add NM policy window on Network Monitor Policies page;
2.Enter a policy name, and select a probe target;

Select TCP or TCP-Explicit Route as probe type;
Enter a port number as below:
0
65536
65535
80

14.result:
 For value 0, firewall will reports an errorPlease specify a port number;
For value 65536, firewall will reports:Error: Probe Port: Data out of bounds (min = 0, max = 65535).
Value 65535 and 80 should be accepted as the correct port number.

16.result:
 For value 0, firewall will reportPlease specify a probe interval;
For value 9999, firewall will report Error: Probe Interval: Data out of bounds (min = 1, max = 3600);
The last three values will be accepted,

17.result:
 For value 0, firewall will report Please specify a reply timeout;
For value 10, firewall will report The probe interval must be greater than the reply timeout.;
For value 80, firewall will report Error: Reply Time Out: Data out of bounds (min = 1, max = 60).
Value 3, 1 and 60 will be accepted by firewall.

